description:
Foundation for all panel view modes. Introduce two orthogonal per-pane enums:

TPaneRole = (prList, prInfo, prQuickView, prSectorMap, prBlockMap, prTree);
TListMode = (lmBrief, lmFull, lmWide);

FPaneRole answers 'what is this pane' (browsing vs companion). FListMode answers 'how is the browser laid out'. The previous FViewMode collapsed both axes and was removed as dead code (DiskBender-dpi).

Work: add FRole/FListMode fields to TPaneState in TTUIController; DrawPane dispatches on Role; lmFull keeps current rendering as default. No new modes implemented in this issue -- this is the substrate the Brief/Wide/Info/etc. issues build on.

GetFileContent and AddFile both compute physical sectors per track as 'FDPB.SPT div 4', which assumes 512-byte physical sectors (FDPB.SPT counts CP/M's 128-byte logical sectors). Breaks on 256-byte-sector formats where the divisor should be 2.

The block-to-(track,sector) math:
  PhysTrack  := FDPB.OFF + ((BlockIdx * SectorsPerBlock + S) div PhysSPT);
  PhysSecIdx := (BlockIdx * SectorsPerBlock + S) mod PhysSPT;
becomes wrong when PhysSPT is computed from a stale assumption.

Fix: derive PhysSPT from TI.NumSectors (already in scope at most call sites) or expose it as a DPB-derived helper. Read and write paths must change together to keep symmetry.
